  "explanation": {
    "short": "Some letters come in pairs: one plain, one with a puff of air. क and ख, प and फ, ब and भ, च and छ, ट and ठ. Hold your hand in front of your mouth: ख, फ, भ, छ and ठ push out a little breath. English speakers hear a \"k\" in both क and ख, but Hindi does not.",
    "more": "The puffed letters are the plain letter with an h: kh, ph, bh, ch (as in \"church\" with a puff), ṭh. Compare काम (kām, work) with खाना (khānā, food), and बहन (bahan) with भाई (bhāī)."
